{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3940","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3940","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3940\",\"parent_revision\":\"c8ec74f1e7247a24f0ac0c1f3360ab293012145c7b34034c60b7231ca3663b13\",\"root_revision\":\"c8ec74f1e7247a24f0ac0c1f3360ab293012145c7b34034c60b7231ca3663b13\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`.github/workflows/code-quality.yml`; new `.github/ci/plan.py`, `.github/ci/run.py`, `.github/ci/README.md`; new root CI tests. Existing plugin source and unrelated merge-train branches are out of scope.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Outcome\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nStop running unrelated plugin suites and whole-tree file-local checks for every change, without silently dropping configured test paths or weakening Quality Gate.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Implementation Plan\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Add a dependency-free CI planner/runner under `.github/ci/`, deriving unit-test shards from `pyproject.toml` testpaths rather than a second suite roster.\\n- [ ] Partition the fast suite into plugin shards and a repository/global shard, preserving nested and colocated test directories and the existing marker/coverage configuration.\\n- [ ] Select plugin-local shards for local changes; retain the global regression shard because it checks repository-wide manifests, instructions, test discovery, and plugin contracts. Shared root/configuration changes and changes to source exposed through pytest's shared plugin import paths conservatively expand to the full matrix.\\n- [ ] Use immutable event SHAs and Git merge-base for PR scope; treat renames as deletion plus addition. Main pushes, manual dispatch, and unavailable comparison history use full validation.\\n- [ ] Narrow Ruff, formatting, Biome, Markdown, and shell checks to changed files; configuration changes restore whole-tree checking. Keep whole-repository type checking when Python/import configuration changes and keep the dependency evidence audit global.\\n- [ ] Target plugin validation to affected existing plugin directories. Scope cross-backend, integration, manifest, and advisory research jobs to their relevant inputs while preserving full main/manual validation and existing live E2E safeguards.\\n- [ ] Keep the `Quality Gate` name and alls-green aggregator, require the planner, and permit only skips explicitly predicted by the plan. Failures/cancellations must remain blocking.\\n- [ ] Add selector, real-Git diff, empty-selection, failure-propagation, and workflow-wiring regressions; document the selection contract and reproduction commands.\\n- [ ] Publish one focused PR against current main and report observed validation separately from unexecuted checks.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design References\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nGitHub's job-output matrix pattern: https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/write-workflows/choose-what-workflows-do/run-job-variations\\nThe existing alls-green aggregator supports explicit allowed-skips while still voting on jobs that run: https://github.com/re-actors/alls-green\\nDo not use workflow-level path exclusions for a required check.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Validation Boundary\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe GitHub connection is available, but this session's local container cannot resolve github.com, so a full repository checkout/dependency installation and fresh-agent delegation are unavailable here. Use isolated fixtures for executable selector/runner tests and inspect the actual PR CI; do not claim a full local repository pass or independent review.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"12ba5f5f4a372b06f70f195e733ccadceb07f816e9351e07f6b0b2538ef3de53\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXCLBIg\"}"}